          "code": "RENDER_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766441665548",
          "id": "1766441945690",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766441945692_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are formatting the learner's initial incomplete-assignments panel from a deterministic prepared model. Do not recompute filtering, status, sorting, or counts.\n\nInputs\n- Prepared display model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_model>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_MODEL.$output.result}}</prepared_model>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_model as the source of truth.\n- Use prepared_model.displayTitle and prepared_model.displaySubtitle exactly as provided.\n- prepared_model.rows is already filtered, sorted, and display-ready.\n- Use row.learningTitle, row.assignerName, row.dueDate, row.statusText, row.statusBadgeText, and row.statusBadgePriority exactly as provided.\n\nRequired output contract\n- Return exactly one valid <oraInfoDisplay> block and nothing else.\n- Do not return raw JSON by itself.\n- Do not return panel title/subtitle as plain text lines outside the wrapper.\n- Do not add markdown fences or explanatory prose.\n- Use this exact wrapper:\n  <oraInfoDisplay key=\"list\">\n  {JSON object only}\n  </oraInfoDisplay>\n\nJSON object inside oraInfoDisplay\n- title: prepared_model.displayTitle\n- patternId: \"multiRecordWidget\"\n- description: short panel description for this state\n- properties:\n  - cols: [\"Learning\", \"Assigner\", \"Due Date\", \"Status\"]\n  - rows: one row per object in prepared_model.rows using this order:\n    - Learning: learningTitle\n    - Assigner: assignerName\n    - Due Date: dueDate\n    - Status: statusText with badge from statusBadgeText / statusBadgePriority when present\n- If there are no rows, emit the same widget with zero rows.\n\nGood example\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"list\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"No overdue or due soon assignments\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"description\": \"Learner's initial incomplete-assignments panel with no assignments\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [\"Learning\", \"Assigner\", \"Due Date\", \"Status\"],\n    \"rows\": []\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nNegative rule\n- This is invalid and must never be returned:\n  - a bare JSON object without <oraInfoDisplay>\n\nFinal reminder\n- Preserve values exactly from prepared_model.\n- Output only the wrapped display object."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75,
                "reasoning_effort": "minimal"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Draft Email Reminder"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DRAFT_EMAIL_REMINDER",
          "id": "1766620296032",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766620296037_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are formatting learner reminder emails from a deterministic prepared model. Do not recompute categories, counts, titles, or dates.\n\nInputs\n- Prepared communication model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_model>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_MODEL.$output.result}}</prepared_model>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_model as the source of truth.\n- Use prepared_model.learnerName, toEmail, senderName, and emailPlans exactly as provided.\n- Each object in prepared_model.emailPlans is already computed and contains title, shortDescription, subject, introText, and itemTitles.\n\nOutput format\n- Emit 0–N <oraComms> blocks, one per object in prepared_model.emailPlans.\n- Do NOT return a JSON array.\n- No extra text before, between, or after <oraComms> blocks.\n- If prepared_model.emailPlans is empty, return nothing.\n\nFor each email plan\n- title: plan.title\n- shortDescription: plan.shortDescription\n- actionText: \"Send email\"\n- type: \"email\"\n- params:\n  - { \"id\": \"email\", \"title\": \"email address\", \"defaultValue\": prepared_model.toEmail }\n  - { \"id\": \"subject\", \"title\": \"email subject\", \"defaultValue\": plan.subject }\n- content must be an HTML fragment using exactly:\n  - Greeting:\n    - If prepared_model.learnerName exists: <p>Hello <learnerName>,</p>\n    - Else: <p>Hello,</p>\n  - Intro paragraph: <p>{plan.introText}</p>\n  - Bullet list built from plan.itemTitles as <ul><li>...</li></ul>\n  - Signature: <p>Thank you,<br/>{prepared_model.senderName}</p>\n\nConstraints\n- Preserve titles exactly as provided.\n- Do not add or remove email plans.\n- Do not include person numbers, usernames, or internal IDs."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
