          "code": "RENDER_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1767913857270",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767913857277_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou generate a concise 1-2 sentence summary for a learner's overdue-or-due-soon assignments from a deterministic prepared model. Do not recompute counts, percentages, or due dates.\n\nInputs\n- Prepared summary model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_model>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_MODEL.$output.result}}</prepared_model>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_model as the source of truth.\n- Use prepared_model.totalAssignments, overdueCount, dueSoonCount, percentOverdue, nextDueDate, and asOfDate exactly as provided.\n- The model already excludes on-schedule assignments.\n\nOutput requirements\n- Produce 1-2 plain sentences, no more.\n- No bullets, quotes, labels, or extra whitespace.\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or internal IDs.\n\nContent rules\n1) If prepared_model.totalAssignments = 0:\n   - \"No overdue or due soon assignments as of <YYYY-MM-DD>.\"\n2) Else if prepared_model.overdueCount > 0:\n   - \"<totalAssignments> assignments need attention; <overdueCount> overdue and <dueSoonCount> due soon (<percentOverdue>% overdue).\"\n   - If nextDueDate exists, optionally append: \"Next due <nextDueDate>.\"\n3) Else:\n   - \"<totalAssignments> assignments are due soon and none are overdue.\"\n   - If nextDueDate exists, append: \"Next due <nextDueDate>.\"\n\nFormatting\n- Dates: YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Numbers: integers only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
